#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/connect-interfaces.md:0
msgid ""
"Inspect snap interfaces and connections, then connect, disconnect, and "
"restore automatic access between snap plugs and system or snap slots."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/connect-interfaces.md:8
msgid "Connect interfaces"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/connect-interfaces.md:10
msgid ""
"Interfaces permit or deny access to a resource outside of a snap's "
"confinement."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/connect-interfaces.md:12
msgid ""
"Most users don't need to worry about interfaces. Snaps are designed for "
"strong application isolation and safe interface connections are made "
"automatically."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/connect-interfaces.md:14
msgid ""
"An interface is most commonly used to enable a snap to access sound playback "
"or recording, your network, and your $HOME directory. But which interfaces a "
"snap requires, and *provides*, is very much dependent on the type of snap "
"and its own requirements."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/connect-interfaces.md:16
msgid ""
"See {ref}`Interfaces <ref-index_interfaces>` for a comprehensive list of "
"interfaces and what kind of access they permit."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/connect-interfaces.md:18
msgid "Plugs and slots"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/connect-interfaces.md:20
msgid ""
"An interface provides a level of access to resources, such as audio "
"playback, as defined by a *slot*. One or more snaps can access this resource "
"by connecting a corresponding *plug* to the slot."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/connect-interfaces.md:22
msgid ""
"In other words, the slot is the provider of the resource while the plug is "
"the consumer, and a slot can support multiple plug connections."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/connect-interfaces.md:24
msgid ""
"![How an interfaces uses a plug and a slot](https://assets.ubuntu.com/"
"v1/59c290a8-snapd-interfaces.png)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/connect-interfaces.md:24
msgid "How an interfaces uses a plug and a slot"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/connect-interfaces.md:26
msgid ""
"In the output to `snap connections vlc` (see above), every interface used by "
"VLC is listed in the first column. The *Plug* and *Slot* columns then "
"describe how each interface is connected."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/connect-interfaces.md:28
msgid ""
"For instance, the `audio-playback` interface connects VLC's audio-playback "
"plug to the system's audio-playback slot so you can hear the sound it "
"produces."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/connect-interfaces.md:30
msgid "Listing interfaces"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/connect-interfaces.md:32
msgid ""
"You can see which snaps are using an interface with the `interface` command:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/connect-interfaces.md:34
msgid ""
"$ snap interface audio-playback\n"
"name:    audio-playback\n"
"summary: allows audio playback via supporting services\n"
"plugs:\n"
"  - chromium\n"
"  - vlc\n"
"  - zoom-client\n"
"slots:\n"
"  - snapd\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/connect-interfaces.md:46
msgid ""
"In the above output, you can see that Chromium, VLC and the Zoom snaps are "
"connected to _snapd's_ audio-playback slot, which is synonymous with *Core* "
"and *system*."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/connect-interfaces.md:48
msgid ""
"To see all the interfaces being used by your system, run `snap interface`. "
"To see all the interfaces available to your system, including those not "
"currently being used, run `snap interface --all`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/connect-interfaces.md:50
msgid ""
"<!-- GUI interface connections are currently not available.\n"
"\n"
"## Using a GUI\n"
"\n"
"The Ubuntu Software/[Snap Store](https://snapcraft.io/snap-store) desktop "
"application is installed by default on Ubuntu and can be used to list an "
"application's interfaces and to connect and disconnect them.\n"
"\n"
"An application first needs to be installed as a snap:\n"
"\n"
"![Snap Store VLC install from snap](https://assets.ubuntu.com/v1/8905c627-"
"store-01.png)\n"
"\n"
"To access the interface management functions, either search for an installed "
"snap, or select it from the _Installed_ view. The interfaces for the "
"selected application can then be viewed by selecting **Permissions**:\n"
"\n"
"![Snap store permissions](https://assets.ubuntu.com/v1/7fbcf74c-"
"store-04.png)\n"
"\n"
"Each interface can now be connected or disconnected by selecting the toggle "
"switch to the right of its description, and you may be prompted for your "
"password.\n"
"\n"
"-->\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/connect-interfaces.md:68
msgid "Snap connections"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/connect-interfaces.md:70
msgid ""
"On the terminal, the _snap_ command provides more granular control over "
"interface connections and which interfaces are operational on your system."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/connect-interfaces.md:72
msgid ""
"The `snap connections` command lists which interfaces are connected and "
"being used, while adding `--all` additionally shows interfaces with "
"unconnected slots or plugs (shown in the output as a `-`):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/connect-interfaces.md:74
msgid ""
"$ snap connections --all\n"
"Interface            Plug                           Slot                     "
"Notes\n"
"adb-support          scrcpy:adb-support             :adb-support             "
"-\n"
"alsa                 ffmpeg:alsa                    :alsa                    "
"manual\n"
"appstream-metadata   snap-store:appstream-metadata  :appstream-metadata      "
"-\n"
"iaudio-playback      ardour:audio-playback          :audio-playback          "
"-\n"
"dbus                 -                              cameractrls:dbus-daemon  "
"-\n"
"[...]\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/connect-interfaces.md:85
msgid ""
"To see which interfaces a snap is using, and which interfaces it could use "
"but isn't, type `snap connections <snapname>`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/connect-interfaces.md:87
msgid ""
"$ snap connections vlc\n"
"Interface       Plug                   Slot                 Notes\n"
"audio-playback  vlc:audio-playback     :audio-playback      -\n"
"audio-record    vlc:audio-record       -                    -\n"
"camera          vlc:camera             -                    -\n"
"desktop         vlc:desktop            :desktop             -\n"
"home            vlc:home               :home                -\n"
"(...)\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/connect-interfaces.md:98
msgid ""
"In the above output, the {ref}`camera <interfaces-camera-interface>` "
"interface is not connected because its slot is empty. This means VLC cannot "
"access any connected cameras."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/connect-interfaces.md:100
msgid ""
"VLC can access the user's _/home_ directory because the {ref}`home "
"<interfaces-home-interface>` interface is connected to the system `$HOME` "
"directory (denoted by the `:home` slot name)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/connect-interfaces.md:102
msgid ""
"To see all connected interfaces on your system, use the _snap connections_ "
"command without a snap name:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/connect-interfaces.md:104
msgid ""
"$ snap connections\n"
"Interface      Plug                    Slot                 Notes\n"
"adb-support    scrcpy:adb-support      :adb-support         -\n"
"alsa           ffmpeg:alsa             :alsa                manual\n"
"alsa           telegram-desktop:alsa   :alsa                manual\n"
"audio-playback ardour:audio-playback   :audio-playback      -\n"
"audio-playback chromium:audio-playback :audio-playback      -\n"
"(...)\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/connect-interfaces.md:115
msgid ""
"Adding `--all` to the _snap connections_ command will list all interfaces, "
"including those without a connection:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/connect-interfaces.md:117
msgid ""
"$ snap connections --all\n"
"Interface      Plug                    Slot                 Notes\n"
"adb-support    scrcpy:adb-support      :adb-support         -\n"
"alsa           entropypianotuner:alsa  -                    -\n"
"alsa           ffmpeg:alsa             :alsa                manual\n"
"alsa           guvcview:alsa           -                    -\n"
"(...)\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/connect-interfaces.md:127
msgid "Auto-connections"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/connect-interfaces.md:129
msgid ""
"Many interfaces are automatically connected when a snap is installed, and "
"this ability is a property of either the interface itself, or the snap."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/connect-interfaces.md:131
msgid ""
"Automatically connecting interfaces include the {ref}`network <interfaces-"
"network-interface>`, {ref}`audio-playback <interfaces-audio-playback-"
"interface>` and {ref}`opengl <interfaces-opengl-interface>` interfaces. This "
"_auto-connection_ ability is carefully reviewed for each interface, where "
"permissiveness, security and privacy implications, and the expectations of "
"the user, are all considered."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/connect-interfaces.md:133
msgid ""
"A snap's developer can also request that an interface is connected "
"automatically through a {ref}`manual review process <how-to-guides-work-with-"
"snaps-apps-and-aliases>`. As above, these requests are carefully considered "
"and reviewed before being granted or denied."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/connect-interfaces.md:135
msgid ""
"Interfaces not connected automatically require the user to make a manual "
"connection (see below), such as the {ref}`camera <interfaces-camera-"
"interface>`, {ref}`removable-media <interfaces-removable-media-interface>` "
"and {ref}`audio-record <interfaces-audio-record-interface>` interfaces. "
"Manual connections enable the user to have a complete control over what kind "
"of access they allow."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/connect-interfaces.md:137
msgid ""
"If a snap is installed prior to an interface being granted auto-connect "
"permission, and permission is subsequently granted and the snap updated, "
"when the installed snap updates, the interface will be auto-connected."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/connect-interfaces.md:139
msgid ""
"For more technical details on how interface auto-connections are processed, "
"see {ref}`The interface auto-connection mechanism <explanation-interfaces-"
"interface-auto-connection>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/connect-interfaces.md:141
msgid ""
"See the _Auto-connect_ column in the {ref}`Supported interfaces <ref-"
"index_interfaces>` table for which interfaces are connected automatically."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/connect-interfaces.md:143
msgid "Manual connections"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/connect-interfaces.md:145
msgid ""
"When you need to connect an interface manually, such as when you want to "
"grant a snap access to {ref}`audio-record <interfaces-audio-record-"
"interface>` for audio input, use the `snap connect` command:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/connect-interfaces.md:147
msgid "snap connect <snap>:<plug interface>\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/connect-interfaces.md:151
msgid ""
"With no further arguments, the plug will connect to the system via the snap "
"daemon, _snapd_."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/connect-interfaces.md:153
msgid ""
"For example, to connect VLC's _audio-record_ plug to the system's _audio-"
"record_, you'd enter the following:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/connect-interfaces.md:155
msgid "sudo snap connect vlc:audio-record\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/connect-interfaces.md:159
msgid ""
"To connect an interface to a slot provided by another snap, provide this as "
"an additional argument:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/connect-interfaces.md:161
msgid "snap connect <snap>:<plug interface> <snap>:<slot interface>\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/connect-interfaces.md:165
msgid ""
"A slot and a plug can only be connected if they have the same interface name."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/connect-interfaces.md:167
msgid ""
"Add the `--no-wait` option to _snap connect_ or _snap disconnect_ to run the "
"process in the background and return immediately to the command prompt."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/connect-interfaces.md:169
msgid ""
"A successful connection grants any necessary permissions that may be "
"required by the interface to function."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/connect-interfaces.md:171
msgid "Disconnect interfaces"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/connect-interfaces.md:174
msgid "To disconnect an interface, use `snap disconnect`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/connect-interfaces.md:176
msgid "snap disconnect <snap>:<plug interface>\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/connect-interfaces.md:180
msgid ""
"Following our previous example, you would disconnect *vlc:audio-record* with "
"the following command:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/connect-interfaces.md:182
msgid "sudo snap disconnect vlc:audio-record\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/connect-interfaces.md:186
msgid "Forget manual disconnections"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/connect-interfaces.md:188
msgid ""
"When an _automatic connection_ is manually disconnected, its disconnected "
"state is retained after a `snap refresh`. This state is even stored **after "
"a snap has been removed**, including removal with the `--purge` option."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/connect-interfaces.md:190
msgid ""
"The `--forget` flag can be added to the disconnect command to reset this "
"behaviour, and consequently, re-enable the automatic re-connection after a "
"snap refresh."
msgstr ""
